<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erich Zeigner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1886–1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Erich Zeigner was a Social Democratic lawyer who became minister-president of the Free State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> in 1923. In October that year he took Communists into his government, and the Reich government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-stresemann">Gustav Stresemann</a> sent troops into Saxony and removed him by decree. Persecuted under the Nazis, he became mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> in 1945 and held the office until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/erich-zeigner.jpg" alt="Erich Zeigner" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roger Rössing / Renate Rössing · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fotothek_df_roe-neg_0000318_003_Portrait_Erich_Zeigners_bei_1._Mai-Feier_Crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
